Falsifies `paging::sv39::distinct_pages_take_distinct_paths`.

The defect: an eight-bit index field under a nine-bit stride, the mirror of the `aarch64`
record's overlap. Each level now reads one bit fewer than its slot holds, so the top bit of
every level's field selects no entry and three address bits become invisible to the walk. The
top half of every table is unreachable and two pages 2 MiB apart share a leaf.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(a, b)`, for any two page-aligned Sv39 addresses differing only in
bit 20 (the top bit of the last level's field). The harness masks its inputs to
`0x0000_007f_ffff_f000`, so such a pair is inside the range it quantifies over.

**The index math is shared and the proof is not.** The `aarch64` record widens the stride's
overlap and the `x86_64` one replaces the mask with a modulo.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/lib.rs b/crates/paging/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/paging/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/lib.rs
@@ -478,7 +478,7 @@ pub trait PageFormat {
     /// [`LEVELS`](Self::LEVELS) so it is right for both a 4- and a 3-level walk.
     fn index(va: u64, level: usize) -> usize {
         let shift = 9 * (Self::LEVELS - 1 - level) as u32 + 12;
-        ((va >> shift) & 0x1ff) as usize
+        ((va >> shift) & 0xff) as usize
     }
 
